{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-luna","packSha":"851c541d09989016bc92605391caf015679fbb5476a81dd31d5d1e405f94fc86","packTokens":3158,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"tpl","tokens":51,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spans","tokens":208,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"answers","tokens":1301,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"sentences","tokens":1544,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":6,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"Map each restated sentence to the original intent spans (I-n) and answers (Q-n) it comes from. A sentence that matches none gets empty lists. Every sentence n must appear once.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spans\" kind=\"intent\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-1\",\n  \"text\": \"Employees can sign in using authorized Folio3 Google accounts and have employee and vehicle profiles populated or registered.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-2\",\n  \"text\": \"Dedicated parking holders can release today's parking and schedule releases up to 30 days ahead.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-3\",\n  \"text\": \"Employees without dedicated parking can receive notifications and claim available spaces first-come, first-served.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-4\",\n  \"text\": \"Use license plate recognition to verify temporary parking authorizations at the entrance and record verification attempts.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-5\",\n  \"text\": \"Track parking utilization and automatically email weekly reports to designated stakeholders.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"answers\" kind=\"answers\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"question\": \"Who receives a push notification when a space becomes available, and what should happen if delivery fails or a recipient has notifications disabled?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Notify all eligible employees without dedicated parking; availability remains claimable in the app even if a push notification is not delivered.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"What exact actions may Parking Administrators perform, especially when a holder's release has already been claimed and requires administrator intervention?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Manage employee and parking records, configuration, and reports; also reverse a claimed release when needed, recording the intervention.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"What application access, if any, does a Security Guard need for entrance verification and recording entry status?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Provide a guard-facing view of verification results and a way to record whether the vehicle entered.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"Can an employee without dedicated parking claim more than one temporary space for the same date, and can they cancel or relinquish a claim before entry?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Allow at most one claim per employee per date, with no user cancellation after a successful claim.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"How should daily/weekly utilization and the overall utilization percentage be calculated, including the denominator and the treatment of released but unclaimed spaces?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Define utilization as occupied spaces divided by total available spaces for each reporting period; report released and claimed totals separately and exclude released-but-unclaimed spaces from occupied counts.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"question\": \"May employees add, update, or deactivate their registered vehicle details after first-time setup, or must changes be made by an administrator?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Employees can manage their own vehicle records; administrators can also manage them.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-7\",\n  \"question\": \"When a claimant has multiple registered vehicles, which plate should be authorized for that temporary parking claim?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Require the employee to select one registered vehicle when claiming; authorize only that plate for the claim.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-8\",\n  \"question\": \"How will entry events for stickered dedicated vehicles be captured for utilization, given that those vehicles bypass system verification?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Have the LPR system record their plate-entry events without requiring authorization verification.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"answer\": \"Approve all 32 requirements as one run.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\",\n  \"id\": \"Q-9\",\n  \"question\": \"Should the 32 requirements be approved as one run despite the estimate of about three runs’ worth of work, or should the one-run scope be reduced?\"\n },\n {\n  \"answer\": \"Allow the administrator to reverse the claimed release and record the intervention, without automatically revoking the claimant’s temporary parking authorization.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\",\n  \"id\": \"Q-10\",\n  \"question\": \"When a Parking Administrator reverses a claimed release, should the claimant’s temporary parking authorization for that date be revoked immediately, or should the reversal be recorded without revoking that authorization?\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-11\",\n  \"question\": \"After a Parking Administrator intervenes to reverse a claimed release, what should happen to the space, given that the claimant’s temporary authorization is not automatically revoked?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Keep the space allocated to the original claimant for that date; record the intervention and do not make the space available to the holder or another claimant.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-12\",\n  \"question\": \"Should this specification define how Parking Administrator and Security Guard role assignments are provisioned?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Keep role provisioning out of scope; assume staff role assignments are handled outside this system.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-13\",\n  \"question\": \"For a temporary parking claim, must the selected vehicle be active, or may an employee select a registered vehicle that has been deactivated?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Require selection of an active vehicle registered to the claimant; deactivated vehicles cannot be used for claims.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"sentences\" kind=\"restated\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"n\": 1,\n  \"text\": \"Require successful Google authentication with a verified corporate email matching an active directory employee before granting an employee session; reject personal Gmail, other-provider, and unmatched accounts.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 2,\n  \"text\": \"Refresh employee profiles and current parking assignments from source records when employees sign in or administrators update those records; deny dashboard access with retry or support guidance if the corporate profile is missing or unavailable.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"text\": \"Populate refreshed dedicated-employee profiles with employee ID, name, dedicated-parking status, assigned floor, and registered vehicle details.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 4,\n  \"text\": \"Require non-dedicated first-time employees without a registered vehicle to register at least one license plate before vehicle-dependent parking actions; show returning employees without a plate the dashboard with a registration prompt while blocking those actions.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 5,\n  \"text\": \"Allow employees to add, update, or deactivate only their own vehicle records, and allow Parking Administrators to manage employee vehicle records.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 6,\n  \"text\": \"Treat dedicated parking as reserved for its assigned employee on operating days unless released, and let the holder release today's space with one action and view its current status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 7,\n  \"text\": \"Allow dedicated parking holders to schedule releases for operating dates within the next 30 calendar dates in the office's local timezone, and make each space claimable at the configured daily release time; today's release is claimable at that time or immediately if released at or after it.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 8,\n  \"text\": \"Allow holders to cancel unclaimed releases; require administrator intervention to reverse claimed releases, record the intervention, preserve the claimant's temporary authorization, and keep the space allocated to that claimant.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 9,\n  \"text\": \"Send push notifications to every eligible employee without dedicated parking when spaces become available, while keeping spaces claimable in the application if delivery fails or notifications are disabled.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 10,\n  \"text\": \"Allocate each released space to the first successfully committed eligible claim, reject competing claims and repeat claims by the same employee for a date, and return refreshed availability on conflicts.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 11,\n  \"text\": \"Return and display the current available-space count to employees without dedicated parking.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 12,\n  \"text\": \"Require a temporary-space claimant to select one active vehicle registered to them, authorize only that vehicle's plate, and reject missing, deactivated, or another employee's vehicle selections.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 13,\n  \"text\": \"Prevent employees from canceling or relinquishing a successful temporary parking claim.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 14,\n  \"text\": \"Assign a parking floor when an eligible employee successfully claims a temporary space and return and display it to the claimant.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 15,\n  \"text\": \"Allow Parking Administrators to manage employee and parking records, operating-day calendars, release-time and report settings, and stakeholder email addresses; restrict administrative actions and report management to authenticated Parking Administrators.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 16,\n  \"text\": \"Ignore pedestrians, motorcycles, and other non-car objects reported by the entrance LPR system for vehicle authorization.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 17,\n  \"text\": \"Record plate-entry events for vehicles with permanent Folio3 parking stickers without requiring authorization verification.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 18,\n  \"text\": \"For non-stickered vehicles, normalize plate case and permitted spacing, require an exact match to a current-day temporary authorization, and activate the green indicator only for a match.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 19,\n  \"text\": \"Fail closed when a plate is unreadable or the camera, indicator, connection, or authorization service is unavailable; keep the green indicator inactive, alert security for service failures, and record failures when service is restored.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 20,\n  \"text\": \"Record each entrance verification attempt's timestamp, plate when available, verification result, and entry status; allow only authenticated Security Guards to view verification results and record vehicle entry status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 21,\n  \"text\": \"At reporting-period close, record unused dedicated parking when the holder neither released nor used the space, and unused temporary parking when the claimant's registered vehicle did not enter.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 22,\n  \"text\": \"Calculate utilization as occupied spaces divided by total available spaces, report released and claimed totals separately, exclude released-but-unclaimed spaces from occupied counts, and provide daily and weekly values with the denominator.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 23,\n  \"text\": \"At the configured Monday report time in the office's local timezone, generate and email the weekly utilization report to configured stakeholders, including unused-parking records, utilization values, released and temporary-claim totals, and utilization percentage.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 24,\n  \"text\": \"Provide Parking Administrators with on-screen parking reports, filters, and CSV export.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 25,\n  \"text\": \"Do not apply automated warnings, suspensions, or penalties based on utilization records.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\nMap the sentences."}